{"id":183219727417250,"type":"artist","name":"Nucleus","artist":null,"year":1969,"weight":20,"info":{"tags":["Jazz Rock","jazz","Progressive rock","Fusion","death metal"],"country":"GB","begin":"1969","end":"1989","kind":"Group","similar":["Soft Machine","Ian Carr","Gilgamesh","Brand X","Hatfield and the North","Mahavishnu Orchestra","Return to Forever","Caravan","Billy Cobham","Embryo"],"disambiguation":"UK jazz collective","img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/0b2eae0f0a12e8c6c12489752ef2f18b/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg","bio":"Nucleus fue un grupo de jazz rock británico, que permaneció activo entre 1969 y 1989. Fundado por el trompetista Ian Carr, una vez que se deshizo su asociación con Don Rendell. En la primera formación del grupo, estaban además el teclista y oboísta Karl Jenkins, el saxofonista y flautista Brian Smith, el guitarrista Chris Spedding, el bajista Jeff Clyne y el baterista John Marshall. Con esta formación, y en su primer año de vida, Nucleus obtuvo el primer premio del Montreux Jazz Festival de 1969"},"works":[{"id":37941418323106,"type":"album","name":"Nucleus","artist":"Nucleus","year":1969,"weight":3,"yt":"dsPQYXyvbSM","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":40863274011446,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Acid Rock","rank":26,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":46133074911653,"type":"album","name":"Elastic Rock","artist":"Nucleus","year":1970,"weight":5,"yt":"8vlWiHBj2l4","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":145636818792428,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Jazz-Rock","rank":112,"scaruffi":null},{"id":235110983059095,"name":"RYM Top — Jazz — Jazz Fusion","rank":151,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":2}},{"id":31376430115330,"type":"album","name":"We'll Talk About It Later","artist":"Nucleus","year":1970,"weight":14,"yt":"jiHcoj9WhpA","src":"books,charts,musthear","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":6523263672